One day, Bananas the healer and his little cat Sticky started exploring
 a deep dark dungeon.  Bananas wasn't at all sure about the whole
"killing monsters who live in a dungeon" thing that he'd heard about,
so he left it up to Sticky.  He had heard about some fabulous shops
down in minetown, so that's where he decided to go.

He reached minetown without killing anything and had a talk to the
friendly priest about where he should spend his money.  The priest
suggested that he donate it to the church and was very persuasive.
Bananas thought his soul could do with a little polish, so he gave the
priest about 4000 zorkmids in ten easy payments.  Feeling so good about

himself now, Bananas thought "Hmmm... Maybe god does want me to
slaughter
these helpless dungeon inhabitants."  So he bought himself a handy
silver
saber and started practising with it.

Having finished shopping, he decided to go back to the dungeons and
spread the word of god (that priest really was a smooth talker).  With
a sack full of meatballs, Bananas made many animal friends along the
way,
although most of them perished once they had been in his service for a
while.  He travelled through the dungeons with his ever changing
menagerie,
until he came to another set of stairs that went up instead of down.
"I'll see where this leads" though Bananas and up he went.

He found himself in a strange series of rooms with many boulders and
pits scattered seemingly at random.  Bananas found that if he pushed
a boulder into a pit, the boulder was no longer blocking his way and
the pit was easily traverable.  After much pushing a straining, he came

to a room filled with monsters.  After defeating the monsters, Bananas
found a strange looking sack.  "This is the perfect thing to keep all
my shopping in.  Hey! It feels lighter already, this is almost like
magic!"  With his new brightly coloured shopping bag, Bananas went
back down the stairs again.

While exploring the dungeon a little gremlin came along, hit Bananas
and chuckled.  Bananas didn't seem too badly hurt, but for some strange

reason he felt very vulnerable all of a sudden.  The good feeling that
he had after giving the money to the priest was gone.  Bananas was most

upset and mightily smote the gremlin in his rage.

Bananas was walking along, and all of a sudden his feet felt very cold.
"Where have my Nike-Air (tm) boots gone?  They allowed me to jump much
further than usual.  Argh! It's a golden naga" *thwack! smack! clunk!*
"That'll teach him to destroy my shoes! Oh no! Here's another one.  I
better kill him before I end up naked and alone." *smack! thwack!*
"Oh. That was easy."  But Bananas confidence was misplaced, as a third
golden naga snuck up on him a little while later and destroyed his
beautiful robe.  "You @#$%!! That was a present from my grandmother!"
"Well... she gave me the gold and I bought it, but that's beside the
point!" *smack* *smack* *smack* "Humph.  That'll teach him to destroy
my things."

Since these golden nagas were giving him so much trouble, he decided
to visit his old friend Hippocrates.  Perhaps he could give some
advise about what to do with those pesky nagas.  But, to make sure
that his god was happy with this change of plan, Bananas killed some
fresh meat and offered it up to the heavens.  To his great surprise
a sword by the name of vorpal blade appeared and he was told to use
it wisely.  Seeing this as a good omen, he picked up the vorpal blade
and read three scrolls of the type that had sharpened up his silver
saber so nicely (+5).  The blade turned blue for a while three times
and Bananas had the strange feeling that if he tried to make it any
sharper he would destroy it entirely.  As the sword was a gift from
God, Bananas didn't think that he would look too kindly upon that,
so he left the sword at its current enchantment (+7).

When Bananas reached Hippocrates house, he was told that an evil
cyclops had stolen Hippocrates' favourite walking stick.  Bananas
reassured his friend that he would find this cyclops and return the
walking stick to its rightful owner.  Hippocrates thanked him and
wished him well on his quest.  Bananas found the lair of the evil
cyclops and went inside.  As he was walking down the stairs, he heard
the cyclops wake up and grab the walking stick.  "That guy sounds
really pissed off!  And he's come to meet me!  I think it would have
been better if he stayed asleep.  I could have just taken the staff
without any problems.  Wait!  That gives me an idea!"  So Bananas
took out his "mega-doze 5000" brand wand and waved it in the direction
of the cyclops.

In an instant, Cyclops was fast asleep.  Bananas mean streak, never
far from the surface these days, appeared once again.  "Stealing from
poor defenseless old men, that sort of thing ought to be punished".
So Bananas gave Cyclops a swift kick in the nether regions.  Kicking
the wrongdoer feel good, so Bananas took out his enchanted sword and
whacked his nemesis with it for a bit.  Despite being a well trained
healer, Bananas wasn't sure when Cyclops drifted from sleep to death,
but he was definite that he was dead now.  "Oh well.  I'm sure he's
done other horrible things too.  He probably deserved it."

While picking up his friend's walking stick, Bananas saw a pretty
little silver bell.  "What the heck... This is my reward for a good
deed done" Bananas rationalised.  He travelled back to Hippocrates
house intending to give back the walking stick, but Hippocrates had
other ideas.  After taking the walking stick Hippocrates said "I feel
better already! I don't need this old stick.  Here Bananas, you take
it with you, perhaps it will bring you luck."

So Bananas took the walking stick and journeyed onwards...



